\name{cellucid_history_branch_apply}
\alias{cellucid_history_branch_apply}
\title{Apply a branch's steps here}
\usage{
cellucid_history_branch_apply(viewer, branch, name, tracker)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{branch}{A branch by its name or its id (history_summary lists them). Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
\item{name}{A name, unique among its kind (compared without case and extra spaces); no length limit. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{tracker}{A tracker by its name or its id (history_summary lists them); the tracker in use when left out. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{branch}, \code{head} (The step shown now), \code{report} (Every step replayed and what became of it).
}
\description{
Apply a branch's own steps again, by name, on top of the step shown, as a new branch (no values are merged; a step that does not apply here is flagged).
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.branch.apply} (History). It moves the viewer's history, as the person's Undo, Redo or a click on a step does: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_branch_apply(viewer, branch = "Main")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
